  "result": "Perfect! The dashboard function is working correctly. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Dashboard Feature\n\n**Function signature:**\n```javascript\ndashboard(invoices, asOf) \u2192 { counts, outstanding, overdue, topCustomers }\n```\n\n**Returns:**\n- `counts`: Object with invoice counts by status (draft, issued, partially_paid, paid)\n- `outstanding`: Total amount still due on issued/partially_paid invoices\n- `overdue`: Object with { count, amount } from overdueInvoices report\n- `topCustomers`: Top 3 customers by outstanding due, as [{ customerId, due }], sorted highest first\n\n**Key Implementation Details:**\n- Counts invoices by their current status\n- Calculates outstanding total from issued and partially_paid invoices only\n- Leverages existing `overdueInvoices()` and `balanceDue()` functions\n- Aggregates customer totals correctly for multiple invoices per customer\n- Returns top 3 customers sorted by due amount (highest first)\n\n**Test Coverage:**\n- 24 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Invoice counting by status\n  - Outstanding calculations (including exclusions for draft/paid)\n  - Overdue metrics aggregation\n  - Top customers ranking and sorting\n  - Edge cases (empty array, few customers, etc.)\n  - Partial payments impact on calculations\n\n**Example Output:**\n```\nDashboard Report\n================\nInvoice Counts: draft:1, issued:3, partially_paid:0, paid:1\nOutstanding Total: \u20ac2,918.26\nOverdue: count:2, amount:\u20ac1,466.26\nTop Customers:\n  1. C-002 - \u20ac1,452.00\n  2. C-003 - \u20ac977.72\n  3. C-001 - \u20ac488.54\n```\n\n**Test Results:** All 404 tests pass (18 new dashboard tests added).",
